WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.399
After 60 years of communism it's hard to know

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:04.640
just how many Cubans

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:05.920
still support the revolutionary ideals

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.280
of Fidel Castro.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.520
There are no free elections or

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.159
independent polls, the state controls the

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.680
media

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:13.600
and shuts down the internet when it

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:15.600
wants. All we know

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.000
is what we're seeing and hearing. And in

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.799
July when thousands of Cubans marched in

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.159
protest

00:01:18.799 --> 00:01:22.159
they were chatting things like ...

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:28.720
And also this:

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.520
The chant is from this song released a

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:37.280
few months ago —

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:41.840
a song that's become the soundtrack to

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.840
people's frustrations.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.840
It's a spin on Fidel Castro's famous

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.840
slogan.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.440
The system right now

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:13.520
isn't working for anyone. So let's get

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.840
into some of the main reasons why,

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.120
starting with the absolute essential —

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.400
getting enough to eat.

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:34.480
In most countries

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.760
food is supplied by a mix of public and

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.319
private industries.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.640
But Cuba's communist system centralises

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:42.560
and controls that whole process.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.640
Farming is already tough enough. There

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.959
are shortages of things like pesticides,

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.080
fuel and equipment — stuff that has to be

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:50.400
imported.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.599
And there's a drought — the worst in a

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.760
hundred years.

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:55.599
Now, the government sets prices and

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.760
production quotas for farmers.

00:02:55.599 --> 00:02:58.959
It collects their produce and controls

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.959
distribution.

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:03.120
But most economists agree that that

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:04.159
kills any incentive for farmers to be

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.560
more productive

00:03:04.159 --> 00:03:07.680
and the whole system is bureaucratic and

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.920
inefficient.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.200
It didn't work in the Soviet Union, it's

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:14.080
not working in Cuba.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.000
What all this

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:28.080
means is that Cuba can't feed itself.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.760
The state has to import something like

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:32.000
70% of food

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.920
and that just got even more expensive in

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.400
the last year. Global prices jumped

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:38.640
40% because of the pandemic. Now

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.799
to buy food on the international market

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.159
Cuba needs foreign currency but it

00:03:40.799 --> 00:03:43.760
doesn't have much of that

00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:45.680
and there's a whole bunch of reasons for

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.319
it — mismanagement by the country's

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.519
leaders,

00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:50.799
for sure, but also the US embargo,

00:03:49.519 --> 00:03:52.720
which those same leaders have

00:03:50.799 --> 00:03:55.760
consistently blamed for the terrible

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.760
state of the economy.

00:04:11.439 --> 00:04:15.680
A full trade embargo was

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.840
first imposed by President Kennedy

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:18.880
after Fidel Castro seized power in the

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:22.479
Cuban revolution.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.280
It's basically a web of laws and

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.199
regulations that banned US companies

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:36.320
from trading with anyone linked to the

00:04:35.199 --> 00:04:38.240
Cuban state.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.759
The sanctions also make it complicated

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.800
for international companies to do

00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:43.120
business with Cuba,

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.479
especially because so much global trade

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:47.280
is done in US dollars

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:49.360
so it has to go through banks in the US.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.199
Cuba still has trade worth hundreds of

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:54.160
millions of dollars with other countries

00:04:51.199 --> 00:04:56.560
like China, Spain and Germany, but the US

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:58.880
embargo makes it all more time consuming

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.800
and more expensive. And because nearly

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:03.120
everything in Cuba is owned and

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:05.360
controlled by the state or the military

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:07.919
the sanctions don't just hurt Cuba's

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:10.160
leaders, they affect the whole economy.

00:05:07.919 --> 00:05:11.199
Under President Obama a lot of sanctions

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.680
were relaxed.

00:05:11.199 --> 00:05:15.680
He even took Cuba off the US list of

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.520
state sponsors of terrorism.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:18.960
But his successor, President Trump,

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:21.199
reversed that policy,

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:23.360
put Cuba back on the terror list and

00:05:21.199 --> 00:05:25.039
added about 200 more sanctions

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:27.120
that target government ministries and

00:05:25.039 --> 00:05:28.960
businesses linked to the military.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:31.360
So far President Biden has kept all

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:32.800
those sanctions and even added some more

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.560
against Cuban officials

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:37.039
after the crackdown on protesters in

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.639
July. What's clear is that Cuba's ability

00:05:37.039 --> 00:05:40.320
to provide for its people,

00:05:38.639 --> 00:05:41.759
which let's face it, is supposed to be

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:43.520
the Cuban model,

00:05:41.759 --> 00:05:45.199
well, that's being squeezed like never

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:47.850
before. And gone

00:05:45.199 --> 00:05:50.800
are Cuba's rich friends.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:55.759
For decades it could count on the Soviet

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:58.319
Union but when it collapsed in the 1990s

00:05:55.759 --> 00:06:00.160
so did Cuba's economy. That was Cuba's

00:05:58.319 --> 00:06:02.639
last big crisis.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:03.520
In the 2000s Cuba found a new friend in

00:06:02.639 --> 00:06:05.919
Venezuela

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:07.120
and benefitted from dirt cheap Venezuelan

00:06:05.919 --> 00:06:11.039
oil to use

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:13.520
and resell. But oil shipments

00:06:11.039 --> 00:06:15.759
are way down because of US sanctions

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:18.479
and the collapse of Venezuela's economy

00:06:15.759 --> 00:06:21.199
and its oil sector. And it's left Cuba

00:06:18.479 --> 00:06:24.560
struggling to keep the lights on.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.240
Because the economy has been so

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:34.960
bad for years

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:36.800
many Cubans have relied on remittances,

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.800
money sent from their relatives abroad,

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:40.400
especially those in the US 

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:42.639
And that's an important source of

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:44.880
dollars for the Cuban economy too.

00:06:42.639 --> 00:06:45.680
But even that tap isn't flowing like it

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.440
used to.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:49.520
Under President Trump companies like

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:50.080
Western Union were banned from sending

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.919
cash

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:53.520
because they work with a bank in Cuba

00:06:51.919 --> 00:06:56.400
owned by the military.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:58.720
So that dried up a big source of cash.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.520
And Cubans can hardly rely on their own

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:01.520
currency.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:03.599
The peso just can't buy them what they

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:05.520
need. It got even worse

00:07:03.599 --> 00:07:07.680
when the government devalued the peso

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.680
back in January as part of a major

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:12.479
currency reform. 

00:07:13.919 --> 00:07:18.639
It's a huge mess. And then

00:07:17.199 --> 00:07:20.479
you add a pandemic

00:07:18.639 --> 00:07:22.160
which has cut off another economic

00:07:20.479 --> 00:07:24.960
lifeline for Cuba —

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:24.960
tourist dollars.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:33.840
This year international visitors are

00:07:29.919 --> 00:07:33.840
down by nearly 90%.

00:07:37.599 --> 00:07:41.360
The other devastating effect of the

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:42.240
pandemic has been on Cuba's health

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.080
system.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:45.520
It's often held up as an example of

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.919
something Cuba's actually done

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:49.840
quite well, at least better than some of

00:07:47.919 --> 00:07:52.080
its Latin American neighbours.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:53.039
But like other sectors it suffered from

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:56.000
mismanagement

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:59.199
and sanctions — and now it's being crushed

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.199
by COVID-19.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.000
And all those pressures, well, they seem

00:08:15.919 --> 00:08:19.120
to have pushed Cubans to speak out

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.280
against their government

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.879
more openly than ever before. But it's

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:25.280
all come at a cost.

00:08:22.879 --> 00:08:28.240
One organisation has recorded at least

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:31.280
700 detentions and forced disappearances

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:32.159
since those July 11 protests. 

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:55.200
The question is: How much

00:08:53.920 --> 00:09:03.360
longer are Cubans

00:08:55.200 --> 00:09:03.360
prepared to wait?

